# DevHub Environment Variables (example)

# Copy this file to .env.local (or .env) and fill real values.
# NEVER commit real secrets. .env.local is gitignored.

# === Local mode (default, byte-identical, no auth wall) ===
# DEVHUB_OPERATION_MODE=local-dev
# DEVHUB_AUTH_PROVIDER=local
# DEVHUB_DB_DRIVER=sqlite

# === Cloud / Multi-tenant mode (devhub-cloud-foundation Path A) ===
# Respect operation-modes spec from archived SDD:
#   cloud: DEVHUB_AUTH_PROVIDER=supabase + DEVHUB_DB_DRIVER=supabase
#          (or postgres-generic if you choose the thin pg driver later)
#   self-hosted: supabase + postgres-generic
#   local-dev (default): local + sqlite  (no vars needed, byte-identical legacy)
#
# This activates with MINIMAL runtime change:
#   - getAuthProvider() from src/lib/auth/provider.js (hexagonal port, already handles local/supabase/fake)
#   - deps.authProvider + async getActor wired in devhub-mcp/server.js (exact CRIT-001 remediation pattern)
#   - Legacy direct createClient for Supabase DB kept (with transition comments); driver-selector marker preferred where possible
#   - 6 workspace.* MCP tools (tools/workspaces.js) now receive authenticated actor from provider + start of withWorkspaceContext/policy for workspace-scoped ops
#   - Backward: unset or =local keeps synthetic local-user + single local-ws + no auth wall + all old tools exact
#
# Fill real values below (service role preferred for MCP). NEVER commit real keys.
# Rollback: delete/comment the three DEVHUB_* lines (or set local/sqlite). Instant, no data loss.
#
# See MIGRATION_CLOUD_FOUNDATION.md for step-by-step, what the foundation gives you,
# seeding your existing data into a workspace, and "fill your Supabase keys here".

DEVHUB_OPERATION_MODE=cloud
DEVHUB_AUTH_PROVIDER=supabase
DEVHUB_DB_DRIVER=supabase

# Supabase (your existing MCP connection — use the same project)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...your-anon-key...
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...service-role-key...   # preferred for server/MCP (bypasses RLS; app policy still enforced)

# For future postgres-generic driver (thin pg, same surface as sqlite for tenancy tables)
# DEVHUB_DB_DRIVER=postgres-generic
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require
# DATABASE_SSL=true

# Optional: pool size for pg driver
# DATABASE_POOL_SIZE=10

# Owner email used for seeding / local ownership (already in your setup)
NEXT_PUBLIC_OWNER_EMAIL=matiastobarsilva12344321@gmail.com

# Other existing vars (SDD, etc.) remain untouched.
SDD_ENABLED=true
